stered by the Health Resources and Services Administration. This program provides grants to support the use of technology that connects different health care professionals to improve access to health care, including specialty care, for certain rural and medically underserved populations.&nbsp;</p><p>The bill explicitly adds dementia care to the types of specialty care that the program may address.</p>","updateDate":"2026-07-16T19:22:45Z","versionCode":"07"}],"title":"Accelerating Access to Dementia and Alzheimer’s Provider Training Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:40:18Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:40:18Z"}
